Practical 9: Decision Tree Based CART Algorithm
Aim: Demonstrate the working of the CART decision tree algorithm using a real dataset and classify a new sample.

Dataset: Wine recognition dataset from Scikit-learn. The model uses Gini impurity to choose splits.
Complete Python program



import pandas as pd
from sklearn.datasets import load_wine
from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split
from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier, export_text
from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, confusion_matrix

# Load the real Wine dataset
wine = load_wine(as_frame=True)

X = wine.data
y = wine.target

# Split the dataset
X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(
    X, y,
    test_size=0.30,
    random_state=42,
    stratify=y
)

# Create the CART classifier using Gini impurity
cart_model = DecisionTreeClassifier(
    criterion="gini",
    random_state=42
)

# Train the model
cart_model.fit(X_train, y_train)

# Predict test samples
predictions = cart_model.predict(X_test)

# Calculate accuracy
accuracy = accuracy_score(y_test, predictions)

print("CART Decision Tree Results")
print("Accuracy:", accuracy)
print("Accuracy Percentage:", round(accuracy * 100, 2), "%")

print("\nConfusion Matrix:")
print(confusion_matrix(y_test, predictions))

# Display decision rules
print("\nDecision Tree Rules:")
print(
    export_text(
        cart_model,
        feature_names=list(X.columns),
        max_depth=3
    )
)

# Create a new sample using median feature values
new_sample = pd.DataFrame(
    [X.median().to_dict()]
)

# Classify the new sample
prediction = cart_model.predict(new_sample)[0]

print("\nNew Sample:")
print(new_sample)

print("Predicted Class:", wine.target_names[prediction])




The exact predicted class and confusion matrix are printed when the code runs. The accuracy shown is the measured result for this split.

Result: The CART decision tree classifier was implemented using the Wine dataset with Gini impurity. The trained tree was evaluated on test samples and used to classify a new sample.
